+/**
+ * The rule head this declaration sits under — the other half of §2.2's key. Walked back
+ * from the declaration to its own opening brace, so a selector that moves down the file
+ * keeps its identity and a bank row survives a rebase.
+ *
+ * READ OFF THE MASKED TEXT, NEVER THE ORIGINAL (pass-3 critique §2.1, an experiment, not an
+ * argument). When the nearest delimiter behind a rule fell inside a comment or a Vue
+ * template, the "selector" WAS that prose — 17 of 79 banked keys — so a retuner could shorten
+ * a shipped length by 140ms and REWORD THE SENTENCE ABOVE IT, and the ratchet, whose key had
